[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Sicilian Alapin"]
[Variation "Sicilian Defense: Alapin Variation"]
[ECO "B22"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "space-advantage,kingside-pressure"]

1. e4 c5 2. c3 e6
3. d4 { Takes the centre. Black's c-pawn can capture it, but then White recaptures with the c-pawn and keeps a strong centre. }
3... d5
4. e5 { Gains space and shuts the bishop on c8 behind its own pawns. The pawn chain from c3 to e5 is a solid base. }
4... Nc6
5. Nf3 { Develops and defends the pawn on e5 at once. }
5... Qb6
(5... Nge7 6. Na3)
(5... cxd4 6. cxd4)
6. a3 { Stops ...Bb4 and keeps b4 available as a pawn break if Black plays ...c4. }
6... c4
7. Nbd2 { Develops the knight and attacks the pawn on c4, which Black now has to look after. }
7... Na5
8. Be2 { Develops and prepares to castle. } 8... Ne7
9. h4 { Gains space on the kingside and prepares h5, which would take the g6 square away from Black's pieces. }
9... Bd7
10. Rb1 { Prepares b4, which would attack the black pawn chain at c4 and open the b-file. } 10... O-O-O
11. h5 { Continues the space gain. The pawn on h5 controls g6, so Black's knight and bishop have fewer squares. } *
